  "result": "Done! I've implemented the VAT summary report. Here's what was added:\n\n**Added to src/reports.js:**\n- `vatSummary(invoices)` \u2014 generates VAT summary by rate\n  - Filters for 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' invoices (excludes draft)\n  - Groups lines by VAT rate across all invoices\n  - For each line: base = lineTotal - discount (after discount applied)\n  - For each line: vat = base \u00d7 rate \u00f7 100 (rounded per line)\n  - Returns array of `{ rate, base, vat }` where:\n    - rate = the VAT rate (21, 9, 0, etc.)\n    - base = sum of taxable amounts at that rate\n    - vat = sum of VAT collected at that rate\n  - **Sorted by rate descending (high to low)**\n  - Handles null/empty arrays gracefully\n\n**Created 15 comprehensive test cases covering:**\n- Empty/null arrays\n- Filtering by status (includes issued/partially_paid/paid, excludes draft)\n- Single and multiple lines per rate\n- Multiple VAT rates per invoice\n- Aggregation across multiple invoices\n- Correct base calculation with discounts\n- Correct VAT calculation and rounding\n- Proper descending sort order\n- Zero-VAT (tax-exempt) items\n\n**Results:**\n- All 214 tests passing (15 new VAT tests + 16 overdue + 183 existing)\n- VAT report is useful for tax reconciliation and regulatory reporting",
